@startuml seq-09-crash-resume
!include style.iuml
title Crash and resume at each boundary of the payment pipeline\n(fault points for test/fault/; C4, C5, C6, C13, C21, C23; nonce-and-crash spike: 127 of 127 kill runs paid once)
autonumber "<b>0."

participant "Tool task\n(wallet~__send)" as Tool
participant "Daemon\n(start-up)" as D
database "Store" as Store
participant "Wallet lane" as Lane
participant "Signer" as Signer
participant "RPC / Base" as Chain
participant "Receipt follower" as Follower

note over Tool, Follower
  |= kill point |= the store holds |= what the restart does |
  | K1 after the admission commit (wallet:queued) | payment Queued, reservation | sign again; nothing was burnt |
  | K2 after signing, before the start commit (wallet:signed) | payment Queued; bytes only in the dead signer | sign again (same bytes: extraEntropy false); nothing burnt |
  | K3 after the start commit, before broadcast (wallet:stored) | Signed, version {raw, hash}, nonce n burnt | broadcast the stored bytes |
  | K4 mid-broadcast or after it, Sent not recorded (wallet:broadcast) | Signed | rebroadcast: "already known" or "nonce too low", then the receipt |
  | K5 after a receipt was read, before its commit (wallet:receipt) | Sent | read the receipt again |
  | K6 inside a fee bump (wallet:replace) | Sent; versions 1..k | append-only: rebroadcast every stored version, newest first |
  | K7 power loss after broadcast | the start commit must have survived | per-commit sync before the effect (C21); else the lane freezes |
end note

== Restart ==
D -> Store : format check; every MIGRATIONS step committed (C23)
D -> Lane : start each wallet's lane only if absent (id from the wallet id, C2)
D -> Follower : start: every stored, unconfirmed entry
Lane -> Chain : eth_getTransactionCount(wallet) at latest and at finalized
Lane -> Store : compare with the ledger and the stored hashes
alt chain count == ledger, or the difference is explained by stored hashes
  Lane -> Lane : continue from the last commit
else unexplained count above the ledger at latest
  Lane -> Store : freeze the lane until finalized decides (C5, C21); the owner is told
  note right of Store : nonce · lane_turn [chain_ahead] → blocked; blocked · finality [above_final] → free
end

== Resume, by what the last commit holds ==
alt K1 or K2: payment Queued
  note right of Store : payment Queued · crash → Queued; nonce signing · crash → free
  Lane -> Signer : sign I at ledger.next
  Signer --> Lane : raw
  Lane -> Store : start commit (re-checks everything as now: a Deny set meanwhile refuses here)
else K3 or K4: payment Signed
  note right of Store : payment Signed · crash → Signed
  Lane -> Chain : eth_sendRawTransaction(stored raw)
  alt not seen before
    Chain --> Lane : hash
  else already in the pool
    Chain --> Lane : "already known" / "transaction already imported"
  else already mined
    Chain --> Lane : "nonce too low"; the receipt of the stored hash exists
  end
  Lane -> Store : Sent
  note right of Store : Signed · broadcast → Sent; Sent · broadcast → Sent
else K5 or K6: payment Sent
  note right of Store : payment Sent · crash → Sent; nonce in_flight · crash → in_flight
  Follower -> Chain : receipts of every stored version
  alt a version has a receipt
    Follower -> Store : Included (that version); the others "replaced"
  else the nonce was used by a transaction the store does not hold
    Follower -> Store : wait for finalized, then Waiting with a card that says what happened (C7)
    note right of Store : Sent · receipt [blk == 'foreign' and blk_fin] → Waiting
  else no receipt yet
    Lane -> Chain : rebroadcast every stored version, newest first
  end
end

== The tool task's rerun ==
Tool -> Store : idempotent rerun under the same key (no second ask)
alt no stored bytes for the key
  Tool -> Tool : the allowed hook re-checks; a refusal is "did not run" (true: nothing left the machine)
else stored bytes exist
  Tool -> Store : read the lane's outcome
  Tool --> Tool : "may have sent" until a receipt decides; never "did not run" (C13)
end
note over Tool, Follower
  x402 boundaries: after the authorization commit and before signing, re-signing gives the same authorization (derived nonce);
  after signing and before the header reaches the box, the stored header is handed (authorized · crash → authorized).
  Shared invariants after every kill: at most one signed transaction per (wallet, nonce) banda chose; no stored bytes without
  a ledger entry; no entry left Signed without the follower; nothing reported "did not run" while its bytes are stored.
end note
@enduml
